      "editorial": {
        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The admission case is the rhythm section as much as James himself. Big People Music lives between jazz harmony, British soul, funk and contemporary R&B; putting James's piano in a small room with Chris Dave's fractured, elastic time and David Ginyard's bass turns those songs into a live groove laboratory rather than a polished album reproduction. Blue Note also frames these as part of James's first U.S. headline shows, giving the booking a useful moment-in-career context without pretending it is a once-ever event.",
          "trip_verdict": "Actively make room for one of the two sets if New York is already in the regional plan and piano, pocket and contemporary jazz/R&B crossover are in the listening thread. The lineup is specific enough to anchor a night in the city, but I would not rebuild the entire DMV-to-NYC trip around it ahead of a rarer farewell, premiere or one-off master encounter.",
